  "2026-10-27T00:30:40.690Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: strict complete3133-item all-status corpus, lifecycle recovery example tracker scope search, and live open/in_progress lists show no active owner for this new review finding. Full live parent data records completed initial intent recovery. This child owns scoped rendered-example replay only. Review: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1608#discussion_r4383854533"
  "2026-10-27T00:35:33.819Z","harness:codex","The new two-tracker control fails before the fix: executing a rendered example from an ambient tracker succeeds, but the explicitly selected item remains unblocked. After prefixing examples with the same canonical bootstrap arguments as the help retry, linked verification passes all20 tests. The control replays both block and unblock via a real shell from the ambient working directory, with the same item ID in both trackers; only the selected tracker changes and ambient history stays identical. Complete typecheck, focused ESLint and documentation links pass. Native Windows and full exact-head checks remain required on the pushed revision."
  "2026-10-27T01:23:52.542Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit review4384162254 correctly identified premature closure relative to the explicit hosted/review acceptance criterion. Reopened through pm; the prior negative control and passing20-test/typecheck/lint/docs evidence remain valid. Only this follow-up is claimed while source-head hosted verification completes. The existing GitHub CI attempt acquired a runner during the guarded requeue check, so no cancel/rerun was performed. No source code or acceptance threshold changes are needed for this correction."
  "2026-10-27T01:31:18.867Z","harness:codex","Hosted source acceptance completed before verified re-closure: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/40427868889 and exact coverage https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/40427868889/job/121952280993 . The canonical receipt has zero failed/pending/missing contexts and matching required publishers; GitHub remains BLOCKED solely by the still-open timing conversation, which is addressed by this recorded reopen/verified-close sequence and will be resolved after it is pushed. No source changes or acceptance/coverage reductions are made."
